e a number of others uh some of  them have excellent names things like  macaroons often food related uh says  something quite a lot about  cryptographers i think  and there are is obviously everyone's  favorite secure messaging software  something that has become an  increasingly major part of our lives and  something that software developers touch  more and more  nowadays your average software developer  is more likely than ever  to have to deploy some form of  cryptography in their applications even  if it's something as small as hashing  some data this is regardless of their  development environment it's regardless  of how you conceptualize yourself as a  software developer it's beyond things  like back end or front end whichever end  you think you operate on you are likely  to have to touch cryptography  for swift we've had a number of  libraries to uh work with cryptography  but the one that has mattered the most  for client developers recently uh is  cryptokit and i'd like to talk about  cryptokit uh just a little bit cryptokit  is a brand new apple system library it  was introduced at wwdc 2019 which i hope  many of you were at  uh this was in the session cryptography  on your apps i've given you a nice  citation there if you'd like to go watch  this session  its goal is to be a swift first  cryptography library that provides  expressive apis for performing  cryptographic operations securely and  efficiently  the particular area of focus here is to  provide high level apis which are  resistant to misuse  and this notion of misuse is something  i'm going to want to come back to later  on in the session  cryptokit takes advantage of many of the  powerful abstractions of swift the kind  of things that we've talked about in  previous dot swift conferences things  like value types things like generics  and things like reference counting  this gives your code powerful tools that  perform well and most importantly are  easy to use and hard to misuse  it's got a lot 